{"chunk_id": "993bc1d57b3c", "text": "The battle between Arjuna and the grandsire Bhishma intensifies as Bhishma overwhelms the Pandava army with relentless showers of arrows. Seeing Arjuna fight too gently, Krishna\u2014enraged by the destruction\u2014leaps from the chariot with whip in hand, rushing toward Bhishma as if to kill him himself, nearly breaking his vow not to fight. Arjuna restrains him and promises to defeat Bhishma. That evening, shaken by Bhishma\u2019s devastation, Yudhishthira contemplates abandoning the war but instead consults Krishna and then Bhishma himself. In an extraordinary moment of candor, Bhishma reveals the key to defeating him: Arjuna must place Shikhandin before him, since Bhishma refuses to fight one who was once female. Arjuna struggles emotionally with the duty of killing his beloved grandsire, while Krishna insists that duty and destiny demand it.\nKrishna nearly breaks his vow to attack Bhishma; later the Pandavas seek Bhishma\u2019s counsel and learn he can be defeated if Arjuna fights him behind Shikhandi.\nThemes: duty vs affection, war ethics, Krishna\u2019s restraint, Bhishma\u2019s honor, strategy of Shikhandi", "vector": [0.0006276083295233548, -0.014116737991571426, -0.0012925086775794625, 0.02958955056965351, 0.009024676866829395, 0.0363156795501709, -0.01627289690077305, -0.007560116704553366, -0.017384877428412437, -0.029752278700470924, 0.017113663256168365, 0.01990717649459839, 0.0029392919968813658, 0.0020883551333099604, 0.0059972405433654785, 0.014116737991571426, 0.045808203518390656, 0.007071929518133402, 0.03967874497175217, -0.022388793528079987, -0.014903261326253414, 0.0011289322283118963, 0.007682163268327713, 0.0014069274766370654, -0.026985887438058853, 0.028992876410484314, 0.016191532835364342, -0.014943943358957767, 0.005197156220674515, -0.017628971487283707, -0.019744448363780975, 0.007071929518133402, 0.001716282102279365, 0.0029918397776782513, -0.04062799736857414, -0.0014145554741844535, -0.0024